servable-universes/frobenius-su2.lean#L39-L39","doc":"The Haar integral is bi-invariant under the 3-dimensional group SU(2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.SU2FrobeniusData.invarianceGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.SU2FrobeniusData.invarianceGroup","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-su2.lean#L37-L37","doc":"Dimension of the group whose bi-invariance is witnessed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.SU2FrobeniusData.haar_normalised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.SU2FrobeniusData.haar_normalised","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-su2.lean#L35-L35","doc":"The Haar integral is normalised: ∫_G 1 dμ = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.SU2FrobeniusData.integralOfUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.SU2FrobeniusData.integralOfUnit","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-su2.lean#L33-L33","doc":"Value of the Haar integral on the unit: ∫_G 1 dμ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.SU2FrobeniusData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.SU2FrobeniusData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-su2.lean#L31-L31","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.SU2FrobeniusData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.SU2FrobeniusData","kind":"structure","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3